# Minimal external library suppressions for ThreadSanitizer (P0-28 audited minimal set)
# Broad suppression race:libQt6Core.so has been eliminated and replaced with strictly scoped rules:
#
# 1. Target: Qt6 QTest internal watchdog thread data race during QTest teardown
#    Reason: Qt's test framework spawns an uninstrumented watchdog thread that accesses stack variables during exit.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to libQt6Test test harness.
race:libQt6Test

# 2. Target: Qt6 QWaitCondition synchronization in precompiled Qt library
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core lacks TSan instrumentation for QWaitCondition futexes (used by QTest watchdog).
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QWaitCondition symbol.
race:QWaitCondition

# 3. Target: Qt6 QTest internal watchdog thread leak at process exit
#    Reason: QTest watchdog thread is intentionally detached and not joined before exit by Qt test runner.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QThread::start (Desk32 production code uses std::thread exclusively).
thread:QThread::start

# 4. Target: PipeWire thread loop internal mutex unlock across threads
#    Reason: libpipewire-0.3 pw_thread_loop locks and unlocks mutex across internal loop/control threads by design.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to third-party shared library libpipewire-0.3.so.
mutex:libpipewire-0.3.so

# 5. Target: Qt6 queued cross-thread event delivery in precompiled distribution libQt6Core
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core lacks TSan annotations for cross-thread event dispatching.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QObject::event symbol.
race:QObject::event

# 6. Target: Qt6 QMetaObject::invokeMethod cross-thread queued functor event lifecycle
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core lacks TSan annotations for cross-thread queued functor delivery.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to Qt internal QFunctorSlotObject, QMetaCallEvent, and QMetaObject::invokeMethodImpl.
race:QFunctorSlotObject
race:QMetaCallEvent
race:QMetaObject::invokeMethodImpl

# 7. Target: Qt6 QObject::moveToThread internal thread-affinity handoff (QQmlThread / QDBusConnection)
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core uses uninstrumented QBasicMutex (futex) to synchronize
#            QObject::moveToThread with QThread::exec() (reinitBindingStorageAfterThreadMove / QBindingStatus cleanup).
#            Desk32 does not call QObject::moveToThread anywhere in its codebase.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QObject::moveToThread symbol.
race:QObject::moveToThread

# 8. Target: Qt6 D-Bus connection manager spawned by QGuiApplication Linux platform integration
#    Reason: Precompiled libQt6DBus / libQt6Core lacks TSan instrumentation and joins QDBusConnection via
#            pthread_clockjoin_np (not intercepted by libtsan), causing missed happens-before at teardown.
#            Desk32 does not link or use Qt6::DBus.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to libQt6DBus shared library.
race:libQt6DBus

# 9. Target: System libdbus-1 lazy initialization invoked internally by Qt6 QDBusConnection
#    Reason: Third-party libdbus-1 lacks TSan instrumentation (dbus_threads_init / _dbus_get_local_machine_uuid_encoded).
#            Desk32 does not link or call libdbus-1 directly.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to libdbus-1 shared library.
race:libdbus-1

# 10. Target: GLib GMainContext wakeup/teardown used internally by Qt6 QEventDispatcherGlib on QThread
#     Reason: Precompiled libglib-2.0 implements GMutex via inline futexes invisible to TSan, causing false-positive
#             fd race reports between eventfd creation, g_main_context_wakeup (write), and g_main_context_unref (close)
#             on QDBusConnection / QQmlThread startup & teardown. Desk32 does not link or call GLib directly.
#     Scope : Strictly scoped to g_main_context_wakeup and g_main_context_unref symbols.
race:g_main_context_wakeup
race:g_main_context_unref
